2.5 Heterozygosity Testing

loci |&gt;
  is_heterozygote()

[1] FALSE  TRUE  TRUE FALSE FALSE


Within a data frame, the same test summarizes observed heterozygosity by stratum:

data(arapat)

arapat |&gt;
  mutate(het = is_heterozygote(LTRS)) |&gt;
  group_by(Species) |&gt;
  summarize(Ho_LTRS = mean(het, na.rm = TRUE))

# A tibble: 3 × 2
  Species   Ho_LTRS
  &lt;fct&gt;       &lt;dbl&gt;
1 Cape        0.107
2 Mainland    0.472
3 Peninsula   0.242

3.2 Writing Population Data
The write_population() function exports a data.frame to various formats:

# Plain text (colon-separated loci)
arapat |&gt;
  write_population(file = "arapat.csv")

# Genepop format, for one species only
arapat |&gt;
  filter(Species == "Cape") |&gt;
  write_population(file = "cape.gen", mode = "genepop", stratum = "Population")

# Structure format
arapat |&gt;
  write_population(file = "arapat.str", mode = "structure", stratum = "Species")

4.6 Optimal Sampling
The optimal_sampling() function estimates how many individuals are needed to capture a given proportion of allelic diversity:

arapat |&gt;
  pull(LTRS) |&gt;
  optimal_sampling(nrep = 99)

