8.10 Genetic Gravity: Direction from an Undirected Graph
Each edge of a Population Graph is symmetric, but the two populations it joins are compared against different neighbourhoods. Genetic gravity reads the direction of gene flow from that difference: edge asymmetries \(\Delta\), a source–sink score \(S\) for every population, the partitioned distance pGD, tests for a directional gradient, and maps of the gravity field. It has its own chapter, Chapter 9, which walks through the analysis from raw genotypes.

lopho |&gt;
  gravity_field() |&gt;
  plot()

9.8 Default behaviour on a real graph
Nothing above is specific to simulated data. For an existing Population Graph the defaults give a complete picture in one line, here for lopho, the Population Graph of the Sonoran Desert cactus Lophocereus.

data(lopho)

lopho |&gt;
  gravity_field() |&gt;
  plot()

10.4 Interactive Leaflet Maps
addAlleleFrequencies() adds allele-frequency pie charts to a leaflet map and follows the standard leaflet pipe pattern. Pre-compute frequencies with frequencies(), build the base map from strata_coordinates(), then pipe into addAlleleFrequencies().

library(leaflet)
library(leaflet.minicharts)

freqs &lt;- arapat |&gt;
  frequencies(loci = "LTRS", stratum = "Species")

arapat |&gt;
  strata_coordinates(stratum = "Species") |&gt;
  leaflet() |&gt;
  addTiles() |&gt;
  addAlleleFrequencies(freqs)





Pass locus = explicitly when freqs contains more than one locus. Width and height of the pie charts (in pixels) are controlled with width = and height =.

11.3 Migration Events
A migration_event pairs a migration matrix with a generation interval, allowing temporal regime changes:

# Low migration for generations 1-50
evt1 &lt;- c("A", "B", "C") |&gt;
  migration_matrix(model = "island", m = 0.05) |&gt;
  migration_event(start = 1, end = 50)

# High migration from generation 51 onward
evt2 &lt;- c("A", "B", "C") |&gt;
  migration_matrix(model = "island", m = 0.20) |&gt;
  migration_event(start = 51)

11.5 Forward-Time Simulation
The simulate_pop() function runs a multi-generation forward-time simulation. Each generation cycle: census, migrate, mate, mutate.

11.5.1 Basic Simulation

result &lt;- pop |&gt;
  simulate_pop(ngen = 20, verbose = FALSE)

result |&gt;
  head()

  ID Population  Loc1  Loc2  Loc3
1  1          A 02:02 02:02 01:02
2  2          A 02:02 01:02 02:02
3  3          A 02:02 01:02 02:02
4  4          A 02:02 02:02 01:02
5  5          A 02:02 01:02 02:02
6  6          A 02:02 01:02 02:02




11.5.2 With Migration

evt &lt;- pop |&gt;
  pull(Population) |&gt;
  unique() |&gt;
  migration_matrix(model = "island", m = 0.05) |&gt;
  migration_event(start = 1)

result &lt;- pop |&gt;
  simulate_pop(ngen = 20, migration = evt, verbose = FALSE)



11.5.3 With Mutation

mm &lt;- mutation_model(rate = 0.01, model = "iam")

result &lt;- pop |&gt;
  simulate_pop(ngen = 20, mutation = mm, verbose = FALSE)



11.5.4 With Mixed Mating (Selfing)

result &lt;- pop |&gt;
  simulate_pop(ngen = 20, selfing_rate = 0.3, verbose = FALSE)



11.5.5 Census Snapshots
Save population snapshots at regular intervals:

result &lt;- pop |&gt;
  simulate_pop(ngen = 100, census_interval = 25, census_dir = tempdir(), verbose = FALSE)

# Snapshots saved as gen_0025.rds, gen_0050.rds, etc.



11.5.6 Complete Worked Example
Simulate drift and migration in a 3-population system, then analyze the outcome:

# Create starting populations
pop &lt;- freqs |&gt;
  make_populations(N = 50)

# Set up island model migration among the simulated populations
evt &lt;- pop |&gt;
  pull(Population) |&gt;
  unique() |&gt;
  migration_matrix(model = "island", m = 0.02) |&gt;
  migration_event(start = 1)

# Run simulation
set.seed(42)
final &lt;- pop |&gt;
  simulate_pop(ngen = 50, migration = evt, verbose = FALSE)

# Analyze structure in the final generation
final |&gt;
  genetic_structure(stratum = "Population", mode = "Gst")

       Locus        Gst        Hs        Ht p.value
1       Loc1 0.10172629 0.4184512 0.4658393      NA
2       Loc2 0.01295521 0.4401347 0.4459116      NA
3       Loc3 0.02723203 0.4628956 0.4758541      NA
4 Multilocus 0.04765294 1.3214815 1.3876049      NA



# Compare diversity before and after
list(Start = pop, Final = final) |&gt;
  lapply(genetic_diversity, stratum = "Population", mode = "He") |&gt;
  bind_rows(.id = "Generation") |&gt;
  group_by(Generation, Stratum) |&gt;
  summarize(mean_He = mean(He), .groups = "drop")

